course: dictionary
lesson: 8893
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. Read «Every night, huge crowds of fish, shrimp and squid swim up to feed near the surface.» Shrimp is a small sea animal here, because it swims and feeds in the sea.
explain: Now read «You little shrimp, you can't reach the top shelf!» The words «you little» and the teasing tone tell you shrimp means a very small person. Always ask what fits: a sea animal cannot reach a shelf.
explain: Shrimp can also be a verb. «We went shrimping at the rock pools» means we caught shrimps. Look at the sentence: when the word is a doing word, like went or caught, it means to catch shrimps.
fact: A shrimp is a small sea animal with a shell, a long tail and many legs.
fact: Many shrimp are cooked and eaten as food.
fact: «Shrimp» can mean a very small person, often used as a teasing name for a small child.
fact: To shrimp means to catch shrimps, as in «go shrimping».
fact: In Australia people often say «prawn» instead of «shrimp».
exercise: «Every night, huge crowds of fish, shrimp and squid swim up to feed near the surface.» What is a shrimp here? | A kind of boat | A very small person | *A small sea animal with a shell and many legs | A shop that sells fish
exercise: «You little shrimp, you can't reach the top shelf!» What does shrimp mean here? | A petrol station | To catch shrimps | A sea animal that swims | *A very small person, said in a teasing way
exercise: Kai says, «We will shrimp in the bay this afternoon.» What does shrimp mean? | To swim very fast | To hide under a rock | To cook a meal | *To catch shrimps
test: «Narwhals dive under the Arctic sea ice to hunt halibut, squid and shrimps.» Which meaning of shrimps fits here? | *Small sea animals that are hunted as food | A shell on the sea floor | A very small person | To catch shrimps with a net
test: «In a test, cuttlefish waited for their favourite shrimp instead of eating a crab at once.» What does this sentence show? | *Cuttlefish waited, which needs self-control | Cuttlefish were too tired to eat | Shrimp can talk | Crabs are never eaten
exam: «A platypus finds shrimps and worms with the sensors in its soft bill.» What is a shrimp in this sentence? | A very small person | *A small sea animal with a shell, eaten as food | A sensor in the bill | To catch shrimps
